# MCSP Continuous Pre-Settlement Scaffolding 0.24

Status: Constructive architecture
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent: Preservation and Pre-Settlements 0.23

## 1. Objective

MCSP SHALL support continuous pre-settlement through semantic scaffolding.

As interpretation becomes richer, MCSP may establish additional qualified commitments without requiring the complete semantic structure or final hardware realization to be known in advance.

The process is progressive:

    determinate condition
      -> initial pre-settlement
      -> scaffold
      -> additional qualified pre-settlement
      -> richer scaffold
      -> realization
      -> qualification
      -> further qualified refinement

Continuous does not mean uncontrolled or automatic.

## 2. Scaffold

A SCAFFOLD is a provisional semantic structure that:
- retains qualified pre-settlements;
- exposes unresolved dimensions;
- permits later extension;
- records applicability;
- records qualification state;
- preserves lineage;
- does not silently convert open dimensions into fixed assumptions.

A scaffold is not necessarily a runtime object.

## 3. Continuous pre-settlement

A scaffold continuously pre-settles by adding qualified commitments as sufficient determination becomes available.

At each step:

    settled := qualified commitments
    open    := explicitly unresolved or realization-variable dimensions

A valid refinement may increase settled structure while preserving legitimate openness.

## 4. Monotonic rule

Where applicability remains unchanged:

    new pre-settlement SHALL preserve prior qualified commitments.

A refinement may add information.

It SHALL NOT silently contradict an earlier qualified commitment.

If contradiction is required, the affected settlement is:
- suspended;
- versioned;
- requalified;
- or replaced by an explicit successor with lineage.

This follows MCSP qualification/versioning discipline.

## 5. Narrowing rule

A later scaffold may legitimately narrow applicability.

Such narrowing SHALL be explicit.

A narrower settlement does not prove the broader settlement false.

Example structural relation:

    broad semantic pre-settlement
      -> narrower device extension
      -> concrete realization

The narrower layer inherits only commitments that remain applicable.

## 6. Open-dimension rule

Orthogonal dimensions may remain intentionally unsettled.

Examples may include:
- host;
- ISA;
- assembler;
- representation;
- position;
- encoding;
- scheduling mechanism;
- transport;
- device implementation.

A scaffold SHALL distinguish:

    PRESET
    CONSTRAINED
    OPEN
    REALIZATION_DEFINED
    UNSUPPORTED
    UNRESOLVED

These are qualification/scaffolding statuses, not kernel ontology.

## 7. Canonical scaffolding

A canonical is a reusable qualified pre-settlement scaffold.

A more specialized canonical may extend another canonical if it preserves inherited material invariants.

Thus semantic construction can proceed without rebuilding meaning from zero.

## 8. Extension scaffolding

Drivers, protocols, devices, operating systems, and applications may add local pre-settlements.

They SHALL declare:
- inherited settlements;
- new settlements;
- open dimensions;
- realization-specific dimensions;
- applicability;
- qualification evidence.

This enables progressive hardware approach without forcing universal device semantics.

## 9. Correspondence reduction

0.23 left CORRESPOND / "matched" unresolved.

Under scaffolding, correspondence need not mean equality.

Two interpreted conditions correspond when they independently satisfy the same material pre-settlement within the relevant applicability.

Provisional:

    SATISFY(A, P)
    SATISFY(B, P)
      -> CORRESPOND(A, B, P)

CORRESPOND is therefore likely derived.

The deeper unresolved relation becomes SATISFY.

## 10. Satisfaction

SATISFY does not mean textual equality or identical representation.

It means that the determinations projected from a realization do not violate the material commitments of pre-settlement P.

This remains qualification vocabulary.

Candidate reduction:

    SATISFY
      := successful qualification against pre-settlement

If retained, SATISFY is procedural rather than kernel ontology.

## 11. Preservation reduction

Then:

    PRESERVE(P, A, B)

can be reduced to qualified satisfaction of the same material pre-settlement across the compared projections, plus any pre-settled cross-condition relation.

Therefore:

    CORRESPOND
    SATISFY
    PRESERVE

need not become pre-semantic primitives.

Kernel remains:

    DETERMINATE CONDITION

## 12. Continuous hardware clearance

Continuous pre-settlement provides a progressive route toward hardware clearance:

    semantic invariant preset
      -> irrelevant dimensions left open
      -> canonical scaffold reused
      -> extensions add only required commitments
      -> realization fills hardware-specific dimensions
      -> projection qualifies inherited settlements

At no stage should implementation convenience silently settle an otherwise open semantic dimension.

## 13. Independence consequence

Host/hardware independence can emerge incrementally.

A scaffold may first be:
    representation-cleared

then:
    assembler-cleared

then:
    ISA-cleared

then:
    platform-cleared

then:
    cross-hardware qualified

Each increase requires evidence.

The semantic scaffold can therefore mature without pretending to have achieved universal independence at its first version.

## 14. Recovery and contradiction

If a later realization disproves a pre-settlement:

    stop reliance on affected conclusion
    preserve evidence
    identify affected scaffold/version
    de-naturalize if necessary
    correct or successor-version the settlement
    requalify affected descendants

Unrelated qualified settlements need not automatically fail.

## 15. Self-scaffolding target

Ultimately MCSP SHALL be capable of using its own qualified semantic mechanisms to scaffold further MCSP definitions.

That is a required part of self-description closure.

Until this is demonstrated, continuous pre-settlement remains an architectural mechanism rather than a closed self-hosting system.

## 16. Current result

Continuous pre-settlement:
    ADMITTED as constructive scaffolding mechanism.

CORRESPOND:
    DERIVED candidate.

SATISFY:
    qualification procedure candidate.

PRESERVE:
    DERIVED qualification relation.

Pre-semantic kernel:
    DETERMINATE CONDITION.

Next:
    formalize machine-readable pre-settlement/scaffold records and attack canonical normalization without relying on names.
